#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# inverse_fourier_transform

#% text
# `inverse_fourier_transform(g, w, t)` gives the inverse Fourier transform `1/sqrt(2 pi) integrate(g*exp(-im*w*t), [w, -inf, inf])` of `g`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# It is computed as `fourier_transform` is, with the opposite sign in the exponent.

#% item
# `fourier_parameters: [a, b]` gives `sqrt(abs(b)/(2 pi)^(1 + a)) integrate(g*exp(-im*b*w*t), [w, -inf, inf])`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A Gaussian:

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(exp(-w^2/4)/sqrt(2), w, t)
#% output
#= exp(-t^2)

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(1/(1 + w^2), w, t)
#% output
#= (1/2)*2^(1/2)*exp(-abs(t))*pi^(1/2)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A band-limited spectrum:

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(unit_step(w + 1)*unit_step(1 - w), w, t)
#% output
#= 2^(1/2)*sin(t)/(pi^(1/2)*t)

#% text
# A pole off the axis:

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(1/(a + im*w), w, t, assumptions: a > 0)
#% output
#= heaviside_theta(-t)*2^(1/2)*exp(a*t)*pi^(1/2)

#% text
# Distributions:

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(1/w, w, t)
#% output
#= -im/2*2^(1/2)*pi^(1/2)*sign(t)

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(1, w, t)
#% output
#= dirac_delta(t)*2^(1/2)*pi^(1/2)

#% text
# Two variables:

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(exp(-u^2 - v^2), [u, v], [x, y])
#% output
#= (1/2)*exp((-1/4)*x^2 - (1/4)*y^2)

#% text
# A Lorentzian and a hyperbolic function in the frequency variable:

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(exp(-abs(w)), w, t)
#% output
#= 2^(1/2)/(pi^(1/2)*(1 + t^2))

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(sinc(w), w, t)
#% output
#= (1/4)*(sign(1 + t) + sign(1 - t))*2^(1/2)*pi^(1/2)

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# `fourier_parameters:` as for `fourier_transform`; with `[0, 1]` the result is the default one:

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(exp(-abs(w)), w, t, fourier_parameters: [0, 1])
#% output
#= 2^(1/2)*(pi^-1)^(1/2)/(1 + t^2)

#% text
# A number for `t` gives the value there:

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(1/(w^2 + 1), w, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.7601734505331404

#% text
# `assumptions:` is accepted:

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(exp(-w^2), w, t, assumptions: t > 0)
#% output
#= (1/2)*2^(1/2)*exp((-1/4)*t^2)

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(fourier_transform(exp(-t^2), t, w), w, t)
#% output
#= exp(-t^2)

#% text
# At a number the value is the integral:

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(1/(w^2 + 1), w, 0.5) - n_integrate(cos(0.5*w)/(w^2 + 1), [w, -inf, inf])/sqrt(2*pi)
#% output
#= -1.093990765754782e-7

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# An undefined function stays a call:

#% cell
inverse_fourier_transform(F(w), w, t)
#% output
#= inverse_fourier_transform(F(w), w, t)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `fourier_transform`, `inverse_fourier_sin_transform`, `inverse_fourier_cos_transform`
